<Definitions>
	<Usage>
		<Line0>Linetype Definitions used in the export of DXF/DWG files using the export tuning file</Line0>
		<Line1>Name attribute specifies the linetype name in DWG/DXF file. Do not use spaces in name as tuning file fields are seperated by spaces. Should not be blank and unique (later wins if duplicate)</Line1>
		<Line2>Count specifies the number of Dash/Dot elements</Line2>
		<Line3>Dash tags specifies the pen-up (-ve float value) or pen-down (+ve float value) or single-dot (0.0 value). All values are in MM. Tags should be sequential</Line3>
		<Line4>Do not use 2 or more dots/up/down commands consecutively in the definitioin</Line4>
		<Line5>Unitless="1" specifies not to scale line definition by 25.4 for Imperial export</Line5>
	</Usage>
